Section One : Vanilla Modifications


[Is Contaminable] | Is not mod reliant
- Allows or Disallows the useage of contamination on Humans.

[Resist Scream] | Is not mod reliant
- Human doesn't care for screams. Does not set off "On Screamed" signals

[GrabbedOnAttack] | Is not mod reliant
- Human can be grabbed by zombies.

[InvincebleOnAttack] | Is not mod reliant
- Turns human invincble on attack, Chance of bugging.

[AllowMultipleAttackers] | Is not mod reliant
- Lets multiple zombies attack.

[VisionFollowTarget] | Is not mod reliant
- Sniper aim/lasers do not chase enemies.

[FleeBeforeZombieExplode] | Is not mod reliant
- Humans run from explosions.

[IgnoreDamage] | Is not mod reliant
- Humans don't notice getting hurt.

[Attitude] | Is not mod reliant
- Fearful, Makes Human act like a civilian.
- Neutral, Human will not chase zombies, Waits for zombie to come to them.
- Aggressive, Human will chase zombies.
- Ignore, Self explanitory.

[RelayAlertOverTime] | Is not mod reliant
- Human can alert other humans.

[AlertRelayRadius] | Is not mod reliant
- How far away Human can alert other Humans.

[AlertRelayRatio] | Is not mod reliant
- Bigger number means more people can be chain-alerted, smaller means less.

[Elevators] | Is not mod reliant
- AttachPassengers, Toggles wether or not passengers stick to it. (dont make the elevatorspeed go above 2 else the human will get stuck when walking)
- Has [DamageType]

[LevelLoader] | Is not mod reliant
- Adds "LoadSpecificLevel" option.

[Extended LevelSize] | Is not mod reliant
- Level Width is extended to 5000. Unfortunately to achieve this, the game wont let you get a height above 250. 
If you know what your doing and edit the LVL file itself you can increase the height that way.
Alternatively if you don't know what your doing, save a copy of the LVL beforehand. (i dont wanna be responsible for you bricking the file somehow)

[Traps] | Is not mod reliant
- Trap Mode, Kill or Damage options.
- Kill Delay, Self explanitory.
- Damage, Self explanitory.
- Damage Rate, How many damage is dealt per Ingame Second.
- Damage Type, Also self explanitory.

[Patroler] | Is not mod reliant
- You can place Waypoints ontop of other Waypoints (amazing I know)
- You can color code signals by holding R, (red) G, (green) B (blue) or Y (yellow) when connecting signals

